      },
      "body": "## Summary\n- `chore: import opencode-pi 1.5.0` — syncs this repo (was at 1.3.0) to the current npm release so the fix applies on top of upstream's latest.\n- `feat: rescue disabled native tool calls` — when a model fires one of OpenCode's disabled native tools, the turn now retries **inside the same OpenCode session** (`--session <id>`) with a corrective prompt restating the `<pi_tool_call>` marker contract, instead of dying with `disabled native tool`. Bounded by `OPENCODE_PI_TOOL_RESCUES` (default 2; `0` restores fail-fast).\n\n#### Motivation\n`opencode/beam-free` (and likely other free-tier models) ignore the marker contract and emit real `tool_use` events for `bash`/`read`. On this machine those calls are *not* permission-refused, so every attempt ended the turn with the `disabled native tool` error — four dead turns in one session before this patch.\n\n#### Test plan\n- [x] `node --test dist/index.test.js` — 97/97 pass, including 3 new tests (rescue success via `--session` retry, budget exhaustion error, `OPENCODE_PI_TOOL_RESCUES=0` fail-fast)\n- [x] Real `pi --mode json` subprocess driven against a scripted fake `opencode` binary: turn 1 `tool_use` violation → retry with `--session sess-1` → `<pi_tool_call>` marker → real `read` toolCall executed by Pi → clean final answer\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)",
